        "original_id": "51bc6ca1-a859-57fa-9c3a-018bcc02eff7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: King Conchobar, Cúchulainn, Queen Medb\n- Places: Ulster, Connacht, Cuailgne, Ireland, Lowland Scotland\n- Concepts: Táin, Scots language, Ulster Scots\n\nFacts:\n- The Táin tells of the exploits of King Conchobar and his chief warrior Cúchulainn, who is called \"The Hound of Ulster.\"\n- The Táin tells of Queen Medb of Connacht invading Ulster to capture the Brown Bull of Cuailgne.\n- Ulster is a province in the north of the island of Ireland.\n- Scots is a Germanic language variety spoken in Lowland Scotland and in parts of Ulster.\n- The local Scots dialect spoken in parts of Ulster is known as Ulster Scots.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
